Mantella NPCs who know where they stand with you.

[center][size=5][font=Trebuchet MS][b][color=#93c47d]FEATURES[/color][/b][/font][/size][/center][table][tr][th]Feature[/th][th]What it does[/th][/tr][tr][td]Marriage[/td][td]From [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/159033]M.A.R.A.S[/url]: status lines, spouses and co-spouses; on M.A.R.A.S 2.x also dating, lover, ex-dating and ex-lover. Proposal odds as a six-step scale, only for NPCs M.A.R.A.S tracks as proposal candidates and never for followers who marry through their own quest. M.A.R.A.S's own chance decides a proposal, rolled once per NPC per game day; no proposal is heard for 7 game days after a divorce or a called-off engagement. Generic spouses such as a married guard get no marriage actions; same-sex courtship needs M.A.R.A.S MCM > Show start dialogue to genders set to All[/td][/tr][tr][td]Marriage actions[/td][td]Accept a proposal, break off an engagement, divorce, settle a marriage crisis. On M.A.R.A.S 0.11.1 a second engagement needs its polygamy (MCM toggle or its polygamy quest). When a step cannot happen, the talk is told that nothing has changed[/td][/tr][tr][td]Yes / No box[/td][td]Each marriage action asks you first, once per game day per NPC and per kind of action. Choosing No also blocks a retry that day, and the talk is told you said no[/td][/tr][tr][td]Affection[/td][td]The NPC can raise or lower their own M.A.R.A.S affection from what is said in a talk: a little or a lot, at most 5 up or down per game day. It never drops the score below 25, so a talk alone cannot start a marriage crisis, and it does nothing during one[/td][/tr][tr][td]Event points[/td][td]Deeds, care and gifts from the World module move the score too, scaled by what wins that NPC over, at most once a game hour per kind and within the same daily limit. Physical closeness is left to M.A.R.A.S when it counts scenes itself (2.x, or 0.11.1 with Lover's Ledger)[/td][/tr][tr][td]Marriage crisis[/td][td]When the spouse joins a talk, the crisis moves to M.A.R.A.S's talk stage and the NPC decides in the talk whether to reconcile or divorce. M.A.R.A.S ends it in divorce after 3 game days. The plain divorce action is not offered during a crisis[/td][/tr][tr][td]Wedding day[/td][td]A spouse knows the wedding date and how long you have been married, for weddings that happen with this module installed[/td][/tr][tr][td]Learn the spouses[/td][td]You can tell an NPC who you are married and engaged to. Only offered when M.A.R.A.S is installed[/td][/tr][tr][td]Family ties[/td][td]From [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/158980]Relations Finder[/url]: parents, children, siblings, spouses, cousins, partners, bosses, employees, enemies and sworn enemies, up to 4 names per kind; dead relatives are marked. With the World module, a relative who died in your playthrough gets the day, close family who died in the last 30 days are grieved, and close family you struck are mentioned[/td][/tr][tr][td]Shared history[/td][td]From [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/158983]Lover's Ledger[/url]: your history together, their favourite acts and their other lovers, and a short talk after a scene where the partner speaks first. Needs an adult framework Lover's Ledger supports (OStim). Skipped if the partner is dead or in combat[/td][/tr][tr][td]Closeness[/td][td]Engaged and married NPCs count as close for the other modules; on M.A.R.A.S 2.x also dating and lover[/td][/tr][/table]
[color=#888888]Each part runs only when its mod is installed. In group talks, if the last speaker cannot take a marriage step, the action goes to the one NPC in the talk who can; with two or more possible, nothing happens. A child, or a spouse, fiance or ex, always speaks for themselves. An affection change is always the speaker's own. Without Mantella's Advanced Actions on, the actions are not offered.[/color]

[center][size=5][font=Trebuchet MS][b][color=#93c47d]REQUIREMENTS[/color][/b][/font][/size][/center][list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/196849]Mantella Living World - Integration Hub[/url] (same version as this module)[/*][*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/98631]Mantella[/url] 0.14, with Advanced Actions on[/*][*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/196214]Mantella - Direct AI Connect[/url][/*][*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/83578]Papyrus MessageBox - SKSE NG[/url][/*][*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/13048]PapyrusUtil SE[/url][/*][*]SKSE_HTTP (comes with Mantella)[/*][*]Optional, each for its own part: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/159033]M.A.R.A.S[/url] 0.11.1 or 2.x (with TT_MARAS.esp), [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/158980]Relations Finder[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/158983]Lover's Ledger[/url], Mantella Living World - World (grief and struck-family lines). The Requirements box on download lists M.A.R.A.S and Lover's Ledger, but the module works without them[/*][/list][center][size=5][font=Trebuchet MS][b][color=#93c47d]BEFORE YOU START[/color][/b][/font][/size][/center][list=1]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/98631]Mantella[/url] 0.14: install it and check that a normal conversation works.[/*][*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/196214]Mantella - Direct AI Connect[/url]: install it below Mantella in MO2 and run its Setup Backend.cmd once (needs Python 3.11). Without it the stock Mantella.exe runs and Living World does nothing.[/*][*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/196849]Mantella Living World - Integration Hub[/url], then the modules you want.[/*][*]API key: your LLM service's key stays in GPT_SECRET_KEY.txt in the Mantella mod folder (in MO2, right-click Mantella, Open in Explorer). A key for another service goes in the file named on the Direct AI Connect page, next to it.[/*][*]Open Mantella's settings page (http://localhost:4999/ui in your browser, only while Mantella is running), go to the Actions tab and turn on Advanced Actions. Many Living World actions (bribe, persuade, marriage steps, positions, map marks and others) only work with it, and it needs a model that supports tool calling.[/*][*]Nothing happens? Living World Main Status in Mantella's settings page lists what is missing.[/*][/list][center][size=5][font=Trebuchet MS][b][color=#93c47d]INSTALLATION[/color][/b][/font][/size][/center][list=1]
[*]Install the hub, then this module.[/*][/list][center][size=5][font=Trebuchet MS][b][color=#93c47d]NOTES[/color][/b][/font][/size][/center][list]
[*]Each part runs only when its mod is installed.[/*][*]To turn off the talk after a scene, type set MRB_AfterSceneTalk to 0 in the console (1 turns it back on).[/*][*]Radiant talks between NPCs get none of these lines.[/*][/list][center][size=5][font=Trebuchet MS][b][color=#93c47d]SOURCE AND LICENSE[/color][/b][/font][/size][/center][url=https://github.com/Abhisek571/Mantella-Living-World-Relationships]GitHub[/url], GNU AGPL-3.0 (Mantella is AGPL-3.0). Unofficial, not endorsed by the authors of the mods it works with.

